{
  "_note": "JSE hardening wave 1 — adversarial-audit pins. ASI never detaches a brace-attached else/while(do)/catch/finally; regex literals lex after return/case/typeof/throw (and stripComments never eats `/*` inside one); a dotted POSTFIX run (`arr[0].x.y` — one ident token) walks per segment, method tail included; `new Date(y, m0, d)` builds a LOCAL date from components (TZ-safe via round-trip getters); non-finite numeric literals survive the compiled executor (`1e999` is Infinity on both); matchAll self-advances past zero-width matches; safeInt SATURATES ±Infinity to ±9e18 (substring/toSpliced clamp toward the end, never index 0); toFixed at ≥2^53 returns the plain string coercion; padStart is bounded at 10 000 like repeat; a leading `//` comment can't turn an expression into `;expr`; flat() takes finite-but-huge depths; non-ASCII numerics (½ ٣) lex as plain op chars on every kernel (no tokenizer stall); parser nesting is depth-capped at 200 (a 250-deep paren tower abandons to null — total, never a blown stack) while 100-deep still evaluates.",
